# Git

Twin prose: `maintainer/agents/git.md`.

## Remotes

- **origin:** `zamdevio/burp-mcp` — this product
- **upstream:** `PortSwigger/mcp-server` — official baseline (fetch/cherry-pick only)

Do not push to upstream. Do not force-push `main` (except a user-requested history rewrite such as a fresh init).

## When to commit

Only when the user asks. Never commit secrets, Burp project files, or `maintainer/temp/` scratch (except `.gitkeep`).
Never commit personal/hunt-specific hosts, usernames, or machine paths in tracked files — use generic placeholders (`example.com`). `.env` stays gitignored.

## Message format

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```text
type(scope): subject

<body: why, not a file list>
```

- **type:** `feat` · `fix` · `docs` · `chore` · `refactor` · `test` · `ci` · `build`
- **scope:** short area (`init`, `repeater`, `proxy`, `docs`, `gradle`, …)
- **subject:** imperative, lowercase, no trailing period, ≤72 chars for the whole first line
- Body: wrap ~72 chars. Skip only for trivial one-liners.

```text
feat(repeater): list and read individual Repeater tabs

Montoya cannot enumerate Repeater tabs; agents need live UI reads.
```

```text
chore(init): seed burp-mcp from PortSwigger mcp-server
```

## Gates

- Do not claim done without `./gradlew test`.
- **MCP / Repeater UI changes:** prefer **live-smoke** ([`live-smoke.mdc`](live-smoke.mdc)) **before commit**. Do not commit those until smoke passes unless the user explicitly asks to commit without smoke.
- Do not `--no-verify` / skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.
- Amend only when the user asks **and** the last commit is ours, unpushed, and not on shared `main` after others pulled.

## History

This repo started as a **fresh init** of a GPL-3.0 derivative of PortSwigger/mcp-server. Credit lives in `docs/origins.md` and upstream notices — not in PortSwigger’s original commit graph.
